initech-bkmv -- real dBASE III PLUS 1.1 date contract

Authority: PRD 6.6 / ADR-0008. DBASE.EXE and its three runtime companions
were copied read-only from dbase3-decomp/mint/work; reference.sha256 pins
their bytes. No sibling-repository files were changed.

Recipe: dbase3-decomp/re/harness-setup.md sections 1-3 and 6.2. Fresh host
directory mounted as C:, CONFIG.DB disables ASSIST/TALK/SAFETY/BELL;
inline ON ERROR, SET ALTERNATE, close alternate and QUIT in every program.
SDL dummy video/audio, dosbox-x -defaultconf -fastlaunch -nopromptfolder
-conf <generated-config> -exit, timeout --foreground -k 5 50; no -silent.
Normal core, 386, 60000 cycles, svga_s3, 8 MB. CMP2 additionally verifies
the result with core=auto/cycles=max. The reproducible recipe pins the
DOS date/time (07/24/1986, 00:00:00); these programs do not print the clock.

Run from the InitechOS root:
  sh harness/diff/dbf_diff/date_contract_mint.sh <absolute-dbase3-decomp-root>
This replays and byte-compares all five captures using real DBASE.EXE.
It never updates a golden. Copyrighted interpreter binaries stay in build/.

DATES.PRG / DATELOG.TXT: initial calendar/blank DTOC probe; comparisons
used blank and dated memvars. CMP.PRG / CMPLOG.TXT: direct CTOD calls,
then stored memvars. CMP2.PRG / CMP2LOG.TXT: independently typed program
with numeric and valid-date controls, explicit space-only blank input,
CRLF source and the alternate CPU core. All three are original captures.

VERIFY.PRG / VERIFY.TXT: second independent verification. A fresh copy of
the existing EDGE.DBF/.DBT input is E7. WHEN is a Date field, replaced with
a blank date, copied to MBLANK; MDATE is 09/07/1985. Both EXACT modes test
all six operators in both orders for CTOD(""), MBLANK and WHEN versus
MDATE, plus all nine blank/blank source pairs for <, = and <=.

DATECHK.PRG / DATECHK.TXT: final expanded verification, extending the
blank/blank pairs to all six operators. Q001..Q036 and Q091..Q126 each
have exactly one blank: EVERY result is .F. Q037..Q090 and Q127..Q180
have two blanks: EVERY result is .T., even <> and >. EXACT has no effect.
The earlier captures agree on every overlapping case. S01/S02 prove the
field/memvar types and values; S03/S04 are non-blank comparison controls.
B01..B03 preserve DTOC separators with CENTURY OFF/ON. C01..C16 cover
calendar rollovers, I5's 13/40/85, zero/outsize month/day, empty input and
the ANSI parser's 08/05/85 -> 1908-07-24. These are real output bytes,
including CRLF and DOS EOF, not reconstructed expected text.

The parent sha256.txt pins all sources and captures. test-samir-datatype
datecontract replays DATECHK.PRG through the shipped dot prompt and
compares every tagged line to DATECHK.TXT. Pure eval/fn-a/setfmt/coercion
gates cite these captures for their literal expectations.

RULING CONFLICT: the 2026-10-24 directive says "follow real dBASE III PLUS
1.1", with a derived "blank date compares LOW" detail. The operator's
clarification for this lane gives the real interpreter priority, requires
the independent verification above, and supersedes that LOW detail.
The observed comparison matrix is not a total order. NDX blank LAST is
a separate contract; no index-order expectations are derived from it.
